      "content": "The escrow agent acts as a neutral third party in the real estate transaction, holding funds and documents securely until all agreed-upon conditions are met. Instead of giving money directly to the seller, you hand it to the escrow agent, who then disperses the funds properly to everyone—buyer, seller, lenders, etc.—once the sale officially closes. This protects both you and the seller by ensuring money is only transferred correctly after the property transfer is complete.",
